[{"id":"VRCE-2-78-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing the forces with banners flying quartered on the banks of the river Gangā, and engaged in carious occupations, the lord of the Nisadas, Guha, said to his relatives ranged around.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.753,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12d722d33728fc6cb3c75a17f5cefa7bbf001fde11f5900dcb60393a0d342ff7","compact":"b2766f050e749a0ded249e760b819a02f0afec15d5a8e02fd577ae6e80e2813b","nasal":"8bf22ad22f781ddb84b9ac457f4f82b22707d1a17f43316335ef7b99ea998559"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-78-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":2,"english":"This mighty host here appears like an ocean. I do not find its end even by thinking of it in my mind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.893,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64fa127c303e52c07fd07157a42830c1eb0b656ba1343b14f85f49840faeabd3","compact":"71c56d1520980d3b5fb2819821d166381108e9d83a0888b1cc13a9c3252b25d2","nasal":"2102536483310609302676e429ffcac675dd9ea0d29689b4b7e802a75e579c9a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-78-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":3,"english":"Surely the foolish Bharata has come hither himself: on his car appears the huge Kovidāra banner. Be like, he will either bind us by nooses or slay us and next Daśaratha's son Rāma banished from the kingdom by his sire.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.364,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-3","DUTT-2-84-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":