ssages over the river.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa0aa35e2618fcd6064c3704773a1d60f5e39826ef745160dcee16d59960e4bf","compact":"cc3ac776fff6d244563af2761e8d8c014628b1b6e4a03b973d0a370f2dcfee2d","nasal":"166690dc28b87ca60f87d7fc9e56c8e1ece385e125ac9d6b8058cd15f957c2e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-78-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":7,"english":"And let hundreds upon hundreds of Kaivarta youths accoutred in mail remain in each of five hundred barks., Guha issued this order.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8797ae305ab2a986e7068a05450eff1d895eb2d0e1c4313944df2da555cbf24b","compact":"bcc10dbe3bb13e0445b44cfe20f039e2a7c74cc75718cbfc07b5a06b10616323","nasal":"2b63c2fecda2a76ac457426228717a55a4fc269c2777fb9d35657df61fb0ea80"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-78-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":8,"english":"But if Bharata be well disposed towards Rāma, this host shall today safely cross the Ganga.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-84-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2078008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b32b92df844fe55a0882765e86413123053f262d109ca161b6cacef3d59712ab","compact":"d5adc8203f0b5186bef69826b8ddf7dfdc1d5a57106fb8aaa1337a1046bd5b03","nasal":"255205001e6de56db85a3244b4752e5d3cbb04f2e2159fc6521bb157a3898595"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-78-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":78,"verse":9,"english":"Having said this, the lord of the Nişādas, Guha, 